{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2698 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d2385d428c11ca771b3d360fa7b23c3eba842e4d15e7688ece547918ac02821b" :edb/db-before-t 2697 :edb/db-after-t 2698 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536010 50 #inst "2026-10-09T12:53:37.983Z" 13194139536010 true] [17592186092172 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379279 13194139536010 true] [17592186092172 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379284 13194139536010 true] [17592186092173 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379271 13194139536010 true] [17592186283844 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379278 13194139536010 true] [17592186379271 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379272 13194139536010 true] [17592186379271 1089 "q-11974" 13194139536010 true] [17592186379271 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536010 true] [17592186379271 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe quadrilateral $Q$ is mapped to the quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ has vertices $(-2,-2),(-3,2),(2,2),$ and $(-1,-1).$ Which of the following are vertices of $Q?$\n\n- $(2,2)$\n- $(0,1)$\n- $(-5,-8)$" 13194139536010 true] [17592186379271 1113 #uuid "caa30782-6ec9-52c9-a9a1-a390c30127b7" 13194139536010 true] [17592186379271 1145 "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${Q}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $Q$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-1-(-2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $Q$ are $(0,-2),(-5,-8),(0,2),(0,-1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139536010 true] [17592186379272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379273 13194139536010 true] [17592186379272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379274 13194139536010 true] [17592186379272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379275 13194139536010 true] [17592186379272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379276 13194139536010 true] [17592186379272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379277 13194139536010 true] [17592186379272 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536010 true] [17592186379272 1041 "selection" 13194139536010 true] [17592186379272 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379276 13194139536010 true] [17592186379272 1110 #uuid "9edcd3d5-e0ec-53f8-aac8-7c1370ec12f0" 13194139536010 true] [17592186379273 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536010 true] [17592186379273 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536010 true] [17592186379273 1111 #uuid "6f7948e4-273d-5c4d-bf11-54a1fbdbd9ae" 13194139536010 true] [17592186379274 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536010 true] [17592186379274 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536010 true] [17592186379274 1111 #uuid "281c8f85-07ff-5d78-b469-b69a22a5a942" 13194139536010 true] [17592186379275 1034 "I only" 13194139536010 true] [17592186379275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536010 true] [17592186379275 1111 #uuid "0bed393d-4bcc-521a-8aef-4312269095f9" 13194139536010 true] [17592186379276 1034 "III 